PART a: GCD of Two Numbers (4 marks)

GCD (Greatest Common Divisor) is the largest number that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder.
Algorithm: Euclidean method — gcd(a, b) = gcd(b, a%b), base case gcd(a, 0) = a.

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int a, b, temp;

    printf("Enter two positive integers: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);

    // Euclidean algorithm using while loop
    while (b != 0) {
        temp = b;
        b = a % b;
        a = temp;
    }

    printf("GCD = %d\n", a);

    return 0;
}

Sample Output:
Enter two positive integers: 36 24
GCD = 12

Trace for gcd(36, 24):
a=36, b=24 → temp=24, b=36%24=12, a=24
a=24, b=12 → temp=12, b=24%12=0,  a=12
b=0 → GCD = 12

